e's wall on row 4 already ran from E4 to H4, and Black was playing underneath it. The engine still wanted C6 at the top left."}, {"turn": 18, "text": "The 12k handed some of it back. F2 lost 11.6 points, and the lead rose from -38.2 to -26.7. The engine preferred D7. Black could not use the chance to turn the game around."}, {"turn": 35, "text": "B3 lost 10.7 points, taking the lead from -12.2 to -22.9. The engine preferred A6. Black was working on the left edge, and by the board before move 46 White had taken A6 and B6 there, and a Black stone had been captured."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py prints groups and liberties and count.py does an area count of the current board pasted in; both only flood-fill the given position, with no candidate moves or lookahead. The other commands just cat files and append a game log to games.md.", "stop": false}}